CORE wide-pointer-encoding
main.c
--wide-pointer-encoding --refine
^\[main.assertion.1\] line 21 I2P dereference reads correct value: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Combining --wide-pointer-encoding with --refine must apply the wide
encoding in the refinement solver as well, rather than silently running
the standard encoding. The integer-to-pointer reconstruction (#8103) is
resolved via the backward-constraint hook in the bv_refinement loop, so
the assertion is proven only when the flag is propagated to
get_bv_refinement().
